    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0232" n="118" xml:id="pg118"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890d.01/66: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-26T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 26, 1922—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 26—8:48 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>215. Reference to Department’s telegram 159 of May 19. In conversation at Foreign
                    Office today question of Syrian mandate was brought up. I was told that at early
                    date our Government would receive proposals.</p>
                <p>Mention was made of Palestine mandate, but there was not the least indication
                    that French Government might raise opposition.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
